  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c80a505f",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "c80a505f"
   },
   "source": [
    "### From Scratch (single feature: GrLivArea)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c2ac64ae",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "c2ac64ae"
   },
   "source": [
    "Extract `GrLivArea` as x and `SalePrice` as y, then standardize x (mean 0, spread 1) so gradient descent trains smoothly."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "21dd8f33",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-08-25T05:59:31.601971Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-08-25T05:59:31.601916Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-08-25T05:59:31.603522Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-08-25T05:59:31.603176Z"
    },
    "id": "21dd8f33"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "x = df['GrLivArea'].values\n",
    "y = df['SalePrice'].values\n",
    "\n",
    "x_norm = (x - x.mean()) / x.std()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2a2513de",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "2a2513de"
   },
   "source": [
    "Train with gradient descent: repeatedly update `theta0` and `theta1` to reduce the cost."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "aa9cba8b",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-08-25T05:59:31.604071Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-08-25T05:59:31.604021Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-08-25T05:59:31.607666Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-08-25T05:59:31.607368Z"
    },
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
    },
    "id": "aa9cba8b",
    "outputId": "dae28ae8-3b6a-4fbd-ca37-be8805194aea"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "m = len(y)\n",
    "theta0, theta1 = 0.0, 0.0\n",
    "alpha = 0.1\n",
    "iterations = 500\n",
    "\n",
    "for i in range(iterations):\n",
    "    y_pred = theta0 + theta1 * x_norm\n",
    "    error = y_pred - y\n",
    "    theta0 -= alpha * (1/m) * np.sum(error)\n",
    "    theta1 -= alpha * (1/m) * np.sum(error * x_norm)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"theta0:\", theta0)\n",
    "print(\"theta1:\", theta1)"
   ]
  },
  {
